  "entity_raw": {
    "name_raw": "Bouncing Spell-Like Ability",
    "definition_type_raw": "Monster",
    "source_book_raw": "Horror Adventures pg. 83",
    "definition_raw": "Source Horror Adventures pg. 83\nYou can retarget one of your spell-like abilities when it fails to affect its original target.\n\nPrerequisites: Spell-like ability at caster level 4th or higher.\n\nBenefit: Choose one of your spell-like abilities, subject to the restrictions described in this feat. You can use the chosen spell-like ability as a bouncing spell-like ability three times per day (or less, if the ability is normally usable only once or twice per day).\n\nWhenever you use a bouncing spell-like ability against a single target and the ability has no effect on it (whether due to spell resistance or a successful saving throw), as a swift action, you can redirect the spell-like ability to target another eligible creature within range. The redirected spell-like ability behaves as if its new target were the original target for the spell-like ability. Spell-like abilities that affect a target in any way (including a lesser effect from a successful saving throw) can’t be redirected in this manner.\n\nYou can only select a spell-like ability duplicating a spell with a level less than or equal to 1/2 your caster level (round down) – 1. For a summary, see Table 3–1.\n\nSpecial: This feat can be taken multiple times. Each time it is taken, you can apply it to a different spell-like ability.\n\nSpell LevelCaster Level1Caster Level202nd4th1st4th6th2nd6th8th3rd8th10th4th10th12th5th12th14th6th14th16th7th16th18th8th18th20th9th20th-\n\n1 Bouncing, disruptive, intensified, lingering, or scarring ability.\n2Fearsome, sickening, or traumatic ability.",
    "links_raw": [
      {
        "anchor_text_raw": "Horror Adventures pg. 83",
        "href_raw": "http://paizo.com/products/btpy9n5a?Pathfinder-Roleplaying-Game-Horror-Adventures\n",
        "href_resolved": "http://paizo.com/products/btpy9n5a?Pathfinder-Roleplaying-Game-Horror-Adventures",
        "source_field": "/entity_raw/publications_raw",
        "context_raw": "Horror Adventures pg. 83",
        "role_hint": "publication",
        "target_entity_type_hint": "publication",
        "target_entity_id_hint": null
      }
    ],
    "sections_raw": [
      {
        "heading_raw": "Prerequisites",
        "body_raw": "Spell-like ability at caster level 4th or higher."
      },
      {
        "heading_raw": "Benefit",
        "body_raw": "Choose one of your spell-like abilities, subject to the restrictions described in this feat. You can use the chosen spell-like ability as a bouncing spell-like ability three times per day (or less, if the ability is normally usable only once or twice per day). Whenever you use a bouncing spell-like ability against a single target and the ability has no effect on it (whether due to spell resistance or a successful saving throw), as a swift action, you can redirect the spell-like ability to target another eligible creature within range. The redirected spell-like ability behaves as if its new target were the original target for the spell-like ability. Spell-like abilities that affect a target in any way (including a lesser effect from a successful saving throw) can’t be redirected in this manner. You can only select a spell-like ability duplicating a spell with a level less than or equal to 1/2 your caster level (round down) – 1. For a summary, see Table 3–1."
      },
      {
        "heading_raw": "Special",
        "body_raw": "This feat can be taken multiple times. Each time it is taken, you can apply it to a different spell-like ability. Spell LevelCaster Level1Caster Level202nd4th1st4th6th2nd6th8th3rd8th10th4th10th12th5th12th14th6th14th16th7th16th18th8th18th20th9th20th-1 Bouncing, disruptive, intensified, lingering, or scarring ability. 2Fearsome, sickening, or traumatic ability."
      }
    ],
